{
  "skillId": "multiply-divide-integers",
  "atomType": "R",
  "theory": {
"intro": "To multiply or divide integers, work out the sign and the size separately, then put them together.",
"facts": [
"For two non-zero integers: same signs $\\rightarrow$ positive; different signs $\\rightarrow$ negative.",
"The size is the usual multiplication or division of the numbers, ignoring their signs.",
"A run of multiplications and divisions has equal priority, so work it from left to right.",
"Multiplying by zero gives zero. Division by zero is not allowed."
],
"steps": [
      "Determine the sign of the answer (same signs give positive, different signs give negative).",
      "Multiply or divide the magnitudes, ignoring the signs.",
      "Write the answer with its sign."
    ],
"workedExamples": [
  {
    "question_text": "Evaluate.\n(a) $(-4)\\times7$\n(b) $(-4)\\times(-7)$",
    "solution_text": "(a) Different signs give a negative answer.\n$4\\times7=28$\n$(-4)\\times7=-28$\n(b) Same signs give a positive answer.\n$4\\times7=28$\n$(-4)\\times(-7)=28$"
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Evaluate.\n(a) $(-63)\\div9$\n(b) $\\frac{-56}{-8}$",
    "solution_text": "(a) Different signs give a negative answer.\n$63\\div9=7$\n$(-63)\\div9=-7$\n(b) The fraction bar means division. The signs are the same, so the answer is positive.\n$56\\div8=7$\n$\\frac{-56}{-8}=7$"
  },
  {
    "question_text": "(a) Evaluate $36\\div(-3)\\times(-2)$.\n(b) Find the missing number: $\\square\\times(-5)=45$. Check your answer.",
    "solution_text": "(a) Multiplication and division have equal priority, so work from left to right.\n$36\\div(-3)\\times(-2)$\n$=-12\\times(-2)$\n$=24$\n(b) Divide the product by the known factor.\n$45\\div(-5)=-9$\nThe missing number is $-9$.\nCheck: $(-9)\\times(-5)=45$."
  }
]
},
